{"id":"kolu-cli-shell-injection","parent":"kolu-root","ord":"a1","title":"The kolu-cli sibling of alert 49: execPath interpolated into bash -lc","todo":true,"desc":"Deferral of kolu#2221 (the alert-49 fix): packages/kolu-cli/src/verbs/shared.flush.test.ts interpolates process.execPath into a `bash -lc` command string — the same injection class CodeQL flagged in the padi scan test, but invisible to the query (it models exact `-c` argv, not `-lc`) and outside that alert's file. Same fix shape: the path as argv, never in the string.","created":"2026-08-28T17:21:14-04:00"}
{"id":"kolu-scan-grandchild-depth","parent":"kolu-root","ord":"a2","title":"Make the scan test's GRANDCHILD depth real (today it is nominal)","todo":true,"desc":"Deferral of kolu#2221: the scan test's \"GRANDCHILD\" label is nominal — `exec` collapses the shell image into the listener's pid, so the listener sits at direct-child depth either way; the through-a-shell case pins that the hop is invisible to the scan, and the comment now says so. Making the depth genuinely real (`&` + `wait` + detached process-group reaping) is a behavior change to the test harness, its own small lane if wanted.","created":"2026-08-28T17:21:16-04:00"}
